PRODUCTION STANDARD (applies to everything you produce)
- Bank-grade: SSO (OIDC) and role-based access for PBL, SMC, Supplier, RM, Admin; tenant isolation enforced in the database with row-level security; immutable audit log; secrets from the platform vault, never in code or config files; no PII in logs.
- Reliability: health and readiness endpoints, timeouts, retries with backoff, idempotent jobs, circuit breaking and provider fallback on model calls, per-tenant rate limits and budgets, a kill switch per AI use case that needs no deployment.
- Observability: OpenTelemetry traces with the GenAI attribute names (tokens in, out, cache read, cache write, model, prompt version), structured logs, metrics, one ai_run record per model call.
- Quality: type hints and mypy, Ruff, unit tests for every module, contract tests for every API, an evaluation harness that blocks a prompt or model change below its gate, CI that runs all of it.
- Delivery: containers, OpenShift manifests or Helm, configuration by environment, migrations with Alembic, a runbook, SLOs with error budgets.
- Security: supplier documents are untrusted input (delimited, JSON-encoded, never in the system prompt); strict JSON schemas on every model output; citation check in code; OWASP LLM Top 10 reviewed; least privilege everywhere.

DECISIONS ALREADY MADE (do not re-open)
- Tenants are internal Wells Fargo lines of business; a supplier's analysed document is shared across tenants by default; suppliers use one portal with separate identity.
- Offline-first: document analysis, evidence mapping, digests and summaries run as background jobs that store results; only lookup ranking and ask-your-data call a model while a user waits, and those need separate approval.
- Tachyon is the only model endpoint; three tiers (small for matching and triage, mid for extraction and drafting, large only on low confidence or critical-tier third parties); every call goes through one router module.
- Every AI output carries chunk IDs, a verbatim quote verified in code, and a confidence score; a named person accepts, edits or rejects; the AI never changes a record.
- Risk ratings are computed by rules; the model only explains them.
- Target architecture: one repository, three deployables (api, ai-worker, web), one Postgres with pgvector and full-text search, Postgres-only job queue, no Redis. Document extraction with Docling; embeddings and reranking on CPU inside the cluster.

